 "final_summary": "The authentication token expiry check was incorrectly implemented, allowing tokens to be accepted at their exact expiry. The fix added a proper expiry validation by comparing the current time (converted to timestamp) with the token's expiry time. This ensures tokens are rejected at their exact expiry second, matching the expected behavior.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/auth.py b/tracker/auth.py\nindex 1e865ef..ee70d21 100644\n--- a/tracker/auth.py\n+++ b/tracker/auth.py\n@@ -48,11 +48,10 @@ def verify_token(token, secret, now):\n         expires = int(expires_part)\n     except ValueError as exc:\n         raise AuthenticationError(\"malformed token\") from exc\n-    if int(now.timestamp()) > expires:\n+\n+    if now.timestamp() >= expires:\n         raise AuthenticationError(\"token expired\")\n     return user_id\n-\n-\n def parse_authorization_header(value):\n     if not value:\n         raise AuthenticationError(\"missing credentials\")\n",
